      }, {
        "text": "CoA produced $1$ mole of acetyl-CoA based on carbon chain length ($N_C / 2 - "
      }, {
        "text": "1$), yielding $8$ moles of Acetyl-CoA per mole of oleic acid ($N_C \u003d 18$),"
      }, {
        "text": " plus $1$ mole NADH and $1$ mole FADH$_2$ \\autocite{brunton202"
      }, {
        "text": "5lecture, pubchem_oleic_nodate}.\n\n\\subsubsection{Amino Acid Catabolism - Mitochondrial Matrix}\n"
      }, {
        "text": "Glutamic acid and pyruvate react to form $\\alpha$-ketoglutarate and alanine when catalyzed by $\\alpha$-alanine aminotransferase"
      }, {
        "text": " \\autocite{lenartowicz_significance_1988}.\n\n\\subsubsection{TCA Cycle"
      }, {
        "text": " - Mitochondrial Matrix}\nEach mole of acetyl-CoA and pyruvate produced $3$ moles NADH, $1$ mole FADH"
      }, {
        "text": "$_2$, and $1$ mole GTP. $\\alpha$-ketoglutarate produced $2$ moles NADH,"
      }, {
        "text": " $1$ mole FADH$_2$, and $1$ mole GTP \\autocite{brunton20"
      }, {
        "text": "25lecture}.\n\n\\subsubsection{ETC - Mitochondrial Inner Membrane}\nThe ETC model assumed $2$ moles ATP produced"
      }, {
        "text": " per mole NADH and $1.5$ moles per mole FADH$_2$. The maximum rate was $100$"
      }, {
        "text": " ATP molecules per minute per ATP-synthase \\autocite{brunton2025lecture}.\n\n\\"
      }, {
        "text": "section{Discussion}\n\\subsection{Strengths}\nThis simulation presented a unified set of researched reaction kinetics, coupling"
      }, {
        "text": " demonstrative code with an intuitive organization of metabolism and scientific sources.\n\n\\subsection{Limitations}\nThis simulation is a prototype"
      }, {
        "text": " based on introductory graduate-level knowledge. Modeling was not based on an exhaustive literature review, and accuracy within the overall pipeline was"
      }, {
        "text": " not the highest priority.\n\n\\subsection{Future work}\nFuture work should focus on removing strong assumptions through deeper literature reviews,"
      }, {
        "text": " adding anabolic processes such as gluconeogenesis, and improving code maintainability.\n\n\\section{Appendix I: Physical Constants"
      }, {
