        "text": "}}} \n\\usepackage{seqsplit} \n\\usepackage{xltabular}\n\\usepackage{thre"
      }, {
        "text": "eparttable}\n\\usepackage{amsmath}\n\n\\title{Discretized, First-Order-Kinetics Simulation"
      }, {
        "text": " of the Catabolism Steps of Major Macronutrients of a Peanut in the Human Body}\n\\author{Jon Sharp \\\\"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    jon.sharp@ucdconnect.ie \\\\\n    UCD Student Number: 2527"
      }, {
        "text": "8680\n    }\n\\date{December 22, 2025}\n\n\\"
      }, {
        "text": "usepackage[style\u003dauthoryear,backend\u003dbiber]{biblatex}\n\n\\addbibresource{references."
      }, {
        "text": "bib}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\n\\maketitle \n\n\\section{Introduction}\nThis paper presents a software"
      }, {
        "text": " simulation prototype of the catabolism of key peanut macronutrients within the human body. The simulation begins with chosen quantities of starch"
      }, {
        "text": ", proteins, and fats in the mouth. It concludes in the mitochondria, with final outputs of produced ATP or energy equivalents"
      }, {
        "text": " from the Tricarboxylic Acid (TCA) cycle and Electron Transport Chain (ETC). The simulation does not include major"
      }, {
        "text": " anabolic steps which influence the fate of peanut nutrients.\n\nA video demo of the simulation is accessible at the following link:"
      }, {
        "text": " \\\\\n\\url{https://drive.google.com/file/d/1iAvv22Su"
      }, {
        "text": "3pxp-vrJf5WH93K_mMKOf0L_/view?usp\u003dsharing}"
      }, {
        "text": "\n\nTo construct this simulation, successful enzymatic reaction rate models have been selected from the literature. Individual catabolic steps are intended"
      }, {
        "text": " to appear realistic. However, the project prioritized learning and qualitative demonstration over quantitative accuracy. As discussed below, strong assumptions made"
      }, {
        "text": " for the simulation model fail to capture the true complexities of metabolism.\n\nFurther sections address simulation construction, models used in each"
      }, {
        "text": " organ and metabolic process, assumptions, and limitations. Most of the theory which influenced simulation design and discussion came from graduate course"
      }, {
        "text": " lecture content \\autocite{brunton2025lecture}. This content has been explicitly cited below only in"
      }, {
        "text": " instances where specific numerical values were used in calculations, but it served as the basis for the majority of the content design."
      }, {
        "text": "\n\n\\section{Simulation Construction}\n\\subsection{Micronutrient Inputs}\n\\label{sec:micronutrient"
      }, {
        "text": "-inputs}\nTo represent a peanut beginning ingestion in the mouth, quantities of carbohydrates, fats, and proteins corresponding to"
      }, {
        "text": " 50 grams of whole peanuts were selected. For simplicity, the model only considered the most prominent of each of these"
      }, {
        "text": " macronutrients in peanuts: starch, oleic acid (monounsaturated) \\autocite{settaluri_"
      }, {
        "text": "peanuts_2012}, and $\\alpha$-arachin \\autocite{cui_peanut_"
      }, {
        "text": "2023}, respectively. All triglycerides were assumed to be triolein.\n\nSee \\nameref{sec:"
      }, {
        "text": "physical-constants} for a complete list of sourced molar masses for these nutrients and other relevant physical constants used in the model"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n\n\\subsection{Organ Pipeline Model}\n\\autoref{tab:organ-metabolizers} shows a list"
      }, {
        "text": " of all considered organs/organelles, alongside each metabolic process within that organ and the processed substrates.\n\n\\begin{"
      }, {
        "text": "table}[h]                                                              \n  \\centering   \n  \\begin{threeparttable}\n  \\caption"
      }, {
        "text": "{Organs, Metabolic Agents, and Metabolites in the Peanut Metabolism Simulator}\n  \\label{tab:organ"
      }, {
        "text": "-metabolizers}                                                \n  \\small\n  \\begin{tabularx}{\\textwidth}{|l|\u003e{\\"
      }, {
        "text": "raggedright\\arraybackslash}X|\u003e{\\raggedright\\arraybackslash}X|\u003e{\\raggedright\\"
      }, {
