      }, {
        "text": ": Software Design Details}\n\\label{sec:software-design}\nThe simulation data modeling was implemented using the"
      }, {
        "text": " Kotlin Multiplatform \\autocite{kotlin_multiplatform_nodate} toolset, popular for developing applications which"
      }, {
        "text": " compile for multiple runtimes. The simulation visualization was created with the corresponding UI framework, Kotlin Compose \\autocite{"
      }, {
        "text": "kotlin_compose_nodate}. The simulation was built and packaged using Gradle \\autocite{gradle_build_"
      }, {
        "text": "2025}, developed using the IntelliJ IDEA: Ultimate Edition\n\\autocite{jetbrains_idea_nodate},"
      }, {
        "text": " and tested on a 2024 Apple Mac mini with an Apple M4 CPU and 24 gigabytes"
      }, {
        "text": " of RAM. While the simulation application has been made available for both macOS and Windows distributions, it has not yet been tested"
      }, {
        "text": " on Windows. \n\nKinetics were numerically solved using a first-order differential equations solver from the Apache Maths Commons Java"
      }, {
        "text": " library \\autocite{apache_commons_math_nodate}. It was configured to use the Dormand-"
      }, {
        "text": "Prince 853 integrator with default parameters \\autocite{apache_commons_dormand_nodate}."
      }, {
        "text": " Optimization of these parameters would likely improve the accuracy of simulation performance. This is a candidate for future work.\n\nAll code"
      }, {
        "text": " and build artifacts from this work are publicly available on GitHub: \\\\\n\\url{https://github.com/j"
      }, {
        "text": "sharp4/PeanutsMetabolismSimulator}\n\nClaude Code was used via a command-line terminal during project development. See \\nam"
      }, {
        "text": "eref{sec:ai}.\n\n\\section{Appendix III: A.I. Usage}\n\\label{sec"
      }, {
        "text": ":ai}\nCommercially available A.I. tools were used to assist with the construction of this simulation and"
      }, {
        "text": " for formatting aspects of this paper. All suggested output was verified by this author. All ideas within the paper and in simulation"
      }, {
        "text": " data design are cited or the original work of this author.\n\nClaude Code was used for code refactoring, assistance with"
      }, {
        "text": " triaging issues within the application, formatting Kotlin Compose visuals, and constructing drafts of tables from information already manually embedded in the"
      }, {
        "text": " code. \n\nGoogle AI Studio was used to extract numerical values, units, equations, and abbreviations from publications into formats"
      }, {
        "text": " usable within Kotlin code, to improve the formatting of LaTeX markup, and to search for the location of known content within publications. It was"
      }, {
        "text": " also used for code debugging assistance and written grammar/proofreading.\n\nArchives of all conversations with Claude Code and AI Studio"
      }, {
        "text": " are available at: \\\\\n\\url{https://github.com/jsharp4/PeanutsMetabolismSimulator"
      }, {
        "text": "/tree/final-video-version/ai-assistance-archives}\n\n\\section{Appendix IV: Illustration Sources"
